# v0.25.10 — escrow settlement passes, energy-rate guard, v11/v12 consensus pins, governance parameter tooling

**Baseline**: `v0.25.9` tagged at `217eaa9742` (2026-10-04). Sections below cover `v0.25.9..7cc552b26c` — 57 commits accrued on `main` after the tag, per the release-tag policy (`AGENTS.md`: the version's changelog is finalised in the tagged commit; later entries go to the next version's log).
**Date**: 2026-10-07.
**Tag**: `v0.25.10` (pending).

### Energy-rate guard stack (SD-7): POST band, refresher refusal, Prometheus export, shared staleness window
- `751b98935d` — `POST /v1/market/native-energy/rate` rejects implausible rates at the door (SD-7: `ait_per_eur_scaled` sat at the stub value 1 for nine days, pricing a one-hour GPU quote at 2 units instead of ~17M): a value outside the env-configured band `ENERGY_RATE_MIN/MAX_AIT_PER_EUR` (defaults **0.5–8.0 AIT/EUR**, bracketing the ~4.0 operating point with 2x headroom) is refused with 400, and an explicit int64 pre-check turns a widened-band overflow into a 400 instead of a 500 on insert (the scaled column is int64, `rate*1e18` — max must stay under ~9.22 AIT/EUR). The attestation refresher `native-energy-rate-refresh.sh` applies the same band (same env keys, same defaults) and **refuses+logs a bad stored rate instead of re-attesting it** — previously it re-posted the stored integer verbatim forever.
- `1d3c06e417` — monitoring exports the rate state as textfile Collector metrics (`aitbc_native_energy_rate_*`): stored value, freshness, last-update age, refused/missing. Alert rules flag the coordinator serving no usable rate.
- `13175eba79` — coordinator and fleet now share one freshness window (**86400 s**, env `ENERGY_RATE_STALE_AFTER_SECONDS`) instead of divergent constants.
- `b43c6d147d` — invariant test: the enforced POST band must fully cover every rate the fleet has ever run, so no in-band historical value is ever refused.
- `29445f2779` — ops runbook for the guard: env knobs, deploy, and rollback.
- `3e25a9cd5b` — deploy fix: the textfile-metrics file is written with permissions node_exporter can actually read (0600 → 0644 fix; SD-7 metrics were silently absent on fleet hosts).

### Escrow settlement pipeline: fee-sweep pass, owed-change pass, release-route changes, billed-legs proof, alerts, signing guard (A4–A7, S-8)
All sweeper work lives in the settlement-mark sweeper's tick and submits at most one transaction per pass through the existing guarded submission paths. Proof source is **sealed chain legs**, never row columns.

- **Fee-sweep pass (A4)** — `ffa8ba1811` adds the periodic pass: the route-emitted `ESCROW_FEE_SWEEP` was unreachable (same sealed-nonce slot lost to the higher-fee release; retry skipped `refunded_amount NULL` rows — both live sweeps had been hand-signed). The pass derives residue `lock − Σ releases − Σ refunds − Σ sweeps` from sealed legs and gates fail-closed on: fee-only proof (residue inside the withheld-fee bound), exact custody equality, proposer-mempool pending guard (nothing submits while any authority/ESCROW tx is pending or the mempool is unprobeable), grace (newest leg older than `escrow_fee_sweep_pass_grace_seconds`, default 300 s), a height floor (`escrow_fee_sweep_pass_min_height`, default **35400** — pre-v11 rows are the operator's custody-census decision), and `escrow_fee_sweep_pass_max_jobs` (50/pass). `ESCROW_FEE_SWEEP_PASS_ENABLED` gates it; `_DRY_RUN` logs without submitting; new counter `blockchain_escrow_fee_sweep_pass_total{result}`. Follow-ups `b822dfcc17 ab6af01226 c8da7450d0 955558803d 2c3e55eb1f 91592c3aa8 bba05473aa c1fb316cb6 5489018319 030ee5c6aa`: config plumbing, dry-run/alerts/`skipped_floor` reason, counters + deploy/rollback docs, protected-row deferral, custody-equality proof-of-life check, per-pass job bound, and zero-value refund legs kept out of the residue sum (v11's post-refund guard row).
- **Release route + owed-change pass (A6/F1b)** — `45a1b81b86`: the route stops signing a change leg (an in-request leg loses the same `(sender, nonce)` mempool slot; a waited-for leg outlives every caller timeout). It submits the release only, commits unmarked, and answers `change_owed_amount`. `208b278f28`: the sweeper's change pass pays owed change on a later tick — flag-gated (`ESCROW_CHANGE_PASS_ENABLED`), dry-run capable, per-job backoff, same pending-guard/custody-equality rules, heal-first marking from a sealed refund leg, and it runs **before** the fee pass so a submitted refund trips the fee pass's own guard — refund and sweep never share a mempool window. `694fdeaac6 c906ab7fb5 411e130c15`: sweeper heal-pass demotion of stale unsealed release marks, env-template/fleet-config-check/alert updates, and the tx-hash-pairing gap (an orphan mark from a dropped re-drive no longer blocks the row).
- **Billed-legs proof (A7)** — `305f2a6b70`: `Escrow.billed_legs` records the route's billed gross keyed by tx_hash; `recompute_release_proofs()` replays the route's own fee rule (protected rows bumped to the signed provider credit; multi-leg jobs refuse). Fee pass, change pass, and the route's sweep retry all gate on the recompute — the inversion bound is removed (it only ever proved round-number synthetic jobs). Legacy `billed_legs NULL` rows stay `deferred_unproven`. `d904db2d64 6e16ddb1af fb6fba7dc5 66fd8c8a6f`: protected-row release sealed-value probe, residue min(), floor under A7, release-side tx-hash pairing fix. `2d69e579ac`: heal `refunded_amount`/`swept_amount` from sealed legs and split `deferred_change_pending` out of `deferred_unproven`. `a72ec34ac2`: energy-floor bump from the signed provider credit.
- **Settlement-signing guard + refusal counter** — `29455df496`: `create_escrow` and `refund_escrow` refuse 503 (nothing submitted, no row) on a node that cannot sign settlement — a follower lock strands escrow the hub cannot see; detail names the settlement node when `HUB_RPC_URL` is set, and followers answer the hub-hint 503 on duplicate creates; the shared predicate `_settlement_signing_ready()` is also called by the release gate. `b1c5ceaaa6`: refusal counter `aitbc_escrow_settlement_refused_total{op}` (op ∈ create/refund/release) incremented at each refusal. `dc40c48599`: pre-creates the counter's three op children at 0 so the very first refusal fires `increase()` instead of appearing as a new series. `272103b18a`: renames the counter into the `blockchain_` prefix family — `blockchain_escrow_settlement_refused_total{op}`. `cd3b0af92c`: the two alerts — `EscrowSettlementRefusedOnHub` (never-event, `scripts/monitoring/aitbc_hub_rules.yml`) and `EscrowSettlementRefusedOnFollower` (`scripts/monitoring/aitbc_rules.yml`). `92fa423b61`: the CLI surfaces the node's 503 detail on escrow create/refund/release (create no longer reports success to scripts on a refusal).
- **Monitoring/tests** — `bc79119eec`: settlement-detector crash on missing tx. `86adfaf9b9`: `check-first-sweep.py` one-off proof checker. `0bc2d73b75`: A6 route contract tests. Alert rules `d84c486934 dc9622b2ed 309dddbb1e` (split `EscrowFeeSweepPassUnprovenRows` vs `EscrowFeeSweepChangePending`, pass-tick staleness). `7cc552b26c`: stale xfail section header corrected.

### Consensus: v11 pin at 35400, v12 authority-parameter value checks and pin at 37500
- `d6fc3aba19` — `state_transition_v11_height` hardcoded to **35400**: env-pinned on all ten node/RPC processes since 2026-10-04, activated fleet-wide **2026-10-05** (all five hosts agreed the transition block's hash). The bake changed nothing in a running process — it covers a process started without the line; `STATE_TRANSITION_V11_HEIGHT` still overrides.
- `49636b264f` — **v12 authority-parameter value checks**: from `state_transition_v12_height`, a `GOVERNANCE_EXECUTE` `parameter_change` to any of the five authority parameters (`governance_executors`, `bond_slash_authority`, `bridge_release_authority`, `escrow_settlement_authority`, `escrow_fee_recipient`) is value-checked — non-empty, canonical `0x`+40-hex addresses, no zero address, no duplicates, single element for the single-address parameters, and at least one `governance_executors` member holding the 360000-unit executor minimum. Below the height every value stays lenient so sealed history replays unchanged; mempool admission mirrors the check through the same helper so the door refuses exactly what apply refuses. Baked-in decisions: A5 floor = `DEFAULT_TX_FEE_UNITS`, chain-side proof-of-possession out (tool-side in the ops entry below).
- `0657f60ef6` — `state_transition_v12_height` hardcoded to **37500**: the env value was set on all five hosts and block 37499 stamped version 11 / block 37500 stamped 12, so the height is consensus; env `STATE_TRANSITION_V12_HEIGHT` still overrides and `None` still disables.
- **Activation**: v11 at block 35400 on 2026-10-05; v12 at block 37500 on **2026-10-07 01:19 CEST** (env-activated ahead of the bake).
- **fleet-config-check note**: `STATE_TRANSITION_V12_HEIGHT` is now baked at 37500 — an absent env line still shows as `<unset>` drift by text comparison only; the check cannot verify remotely that a host runs the baked build.

### Ops tooling: executor-signed parameter-change tool with fee-balance and custody-proof gates
- `9c2748a92b` — `scripts/ops/governance_parameter_change.py`: the five authority parameters change only through a `GOVERNANCE_EXECUTE` signed by an on-chain executor key held off-fleet; the node-side execute route signs with the node key and cannot speak for it. The tool builds the sealed-shape envelope and either **plans** (keyless — prints the signing digest for audit) or **signs + submits** (`--key-file`, `--confirm` required) to `/rpc/transaction`, then waits for the seal and reads the parameter back. Refuses non-0x and zero-address targets, no-op changes, unknown parameters, and keys outside the on-chain executor set; key material never reaches argv or output.
- `c837a1391c` — fee-balance gate (sign-submit refuses an executor whose balance cannot cover fee + 5x headroom; covers the proof key on rotation) and an **apply-path rehearsal**: the envelope runs through the real state transition on an in-memory chain — execute applies and reads back, the old authority is refused at activation height, and a self-excluding executor list seals fine on-chain (lock-out refusal is the tool's job, not consensus).
- `47c60ef016` — `--proof-key-file` is repeatable and derives one address per file; sign-submit **refuses a `governance_executors` change unless every added member is proven by custody** (an unproven entry could be a key nobody holds) and a dropped signer with no proven survivor. Every unique proven member is fee-checked. Plan stays advisory (`added — proof REQUIRED` warnings); the rehearsal covers a two-executor rotation.
- `2e5e8e2a87` — plan collects out-of-list proof derivations as warnings instead of hard-failing (read-only command must not exit on malformed input); sign-submit keeps the hard refusal.
- **Live use**: governance executor rotation executed via this tool — `GOVERNANCE_EXECUTE` sealed at block **37259** setting the two-member executor list (2026-10-07, ahead of the v12 checks' activation at 37500 — the same semantic shape the v12 helper later encodes).

### Deploy/update hardening, monitoring fixes, runbook and misc
Prompted by the 2026-10-04 update that unlinked the monitoring units fleet-wide while health reported clean.
- `89ff54f953` — `link-systemd.sh` no longer blanket-deletes every `aitbc-*` unit: monitoring units are modeled per role (escrow-settlements + journal-errors base, authority-balances hub, prometheus-watch followers, island-subscription-check env-gated); the sweep removes DISABLED units, dangling links and role-excluded units but **preserves unmodeled repo-linked units** (operator-managed) and foreign files; orphan timers dropped; `AITBC_ETC_DIR`/`AITBC_BLOCKCHAIN_ENV_FILE` sandboxing. New `test_link_systemd_preserve.sh` runs the real script per role.
- `7e06dd828f` — `update.sh` aborts when the relink drops any previously-present `aitbc-*` unit not in `DISABLED_SERVICES` (a deliberate demotion must be named); `health_check.sh` counts every failed `aitbc-*` unit as an error so the summary can't print "clean" over one.
- `95063e2543` — `update.sh --gitea` resolves explicit arg → `AITBC_GITEA_REMOTE` → `gitea` remote → `origin`, and refuses `.invalid` placeholder URLs before pulling (setup.sh same); island-subscription-check loses scrub defaults — `ISLAND_ID`/`COORDINATOR_URL` now required via its env file; no more placeholder `GOSSIP_WEBSOCKET_URL` written into live env.
- `70b91b49e3` — `update.sh` exits after `main` so a self-rewriting `git pull` can't resume mid-file and execute stray bytes.
- `e889ae9df0` — memory-monitor guards `systemctl show` output (`[not set]`/`infinity` → "no limit", non-numeric current → skip, v1 `MemoryLimit` fallback) and strips the `●` attention marker from unit names; `set -euo pipefail` added.
- `e4695e7eea` — executable runbook for the operator-decided legacy escrow residue payout (Option A): one authority-signed `ESCROW_RELEASE` per legacy custody account, tx-derived census (13 accounts / 2,362,184 units at head 35284), abort/rollback and v11 nonce-collision scheduling.
- `49e70101e2` `833391bad1` — retired openclaw brand stub dropped; default `dao_name` aligned with AITBC defaults.
